    "body": "@annevk that's correct, Chromium's IDL generator was modified slightly in order to avoid throwing in these cases. That was the tradeoff needed in order to eliminate a lot of custom binding code. Here's the actual getContext definition in Chromium's IDL:\r\nhttps://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/modules/canvas/htmlcanvas/HTMLCanvasElementModule.idl?sq=package:chromium&dr&l=16\r\n\r\nand the definition of the \"PermissiveDictionaryConversion\" extended IDL attribute:\r\nhttps://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/bindings/IDLExtendedAttributes.md?l=1456\r\n\r\nNot sure what the best approach in the actual spec should be. Of course it's ideal if browsers use the spec's IDL, but eliminating the custom code for this method is a large benefit.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
