    "created_at": "2018-01-18T08:16:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-18T08:16:44Z",
    "body": "So the unique dictionary thing we have here is treating non-objects as undefined/null.\r\n\r\nThe other thing we have, where the type of dictionary depends on the first argument (though we have no conflicts thus far so could use a single dictionary) is becoming somewhat of a pattern. We could try to stick to a single dictionary, but we've had requests to expose these attributes from the rendering context as well and that point exposing the WebGL attributes on the 2D context would be weird.\r\n\r\n@jyasskin @tobie thoughts?",
