    "updated_at": "2018-01-18T09:53:16Z",
    "body": "So thinking about it some more I think the current solution is still the best, where prose invokes the IDL algorithm and ignores non-objects.\r\n\r\nUnless for some reason we do not want to fix #3182 and foresee that we will never want overlapping names between the various contexts, which seems unlikely.\r\n\r\n(The pattern other specifications appear to have is different, in that one of the dictionary members determines the type. So you effectively have to coerce it twice. Once to determine the type, then again to get the members for that type.)",
