    "body": "@kenrussell that is true and although I thought my proposal was not observable different from what Chrome implements it actually is. (You can observe which dictionary members get consulted.)\r\n\r\nHaving said that, I think we want to keep the non-object check in prose and not add a new IDL extended attribute for that. Chrome implementing it that way is fine though as it's not observably different.\r\n\r\nGiven that, my suggestion would be to merge this and open a new issue on using a unified dictionary for the second argument of `getContext()` and see if others are on board with that or not. (Gecko currently defines it as `optional any contextOptions = null` so some simplification does indeed seem in order here.)",
